
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Host-side unit tests (pure logic, no hardware) can be built and run directly
with the system compiler. GT911 touch coordinate translation:

    cc -I src test/test_touch_coords.c src/touch_coords.c -o /tmp/tt && /tmp/tt

Setup fields (the portal, serial and BLE share them) and the flat JSON reader
behind the serial setup. On a Mac whose Command Line Tools SDK is out of step
with the linker, point cc at Xcode's SDK (DEVELOPER_DIR / SDKROOT):

    cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I src test/test_setup_fields.c src/setup_fields.c -o /tmp/tsf && /tmp/tsf

Physical-button frame/status delivery contract:

    cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I src test/test_button_report.c src/button_report.c -o /tmp/tbr && /tmp/tbr

Signed OTA descriptor + manifest verification (installs the pinned Monocypher
dependency, then runs RFC 8032 + Tesserae fixture vectors):

    sh tools/test_ota_verify.sh

Frame-cache collection manifest, cache differ, and offline Album playback:

    sh tools/test_frame_collection.sh

Device log capture (RTC ring, redaction, upload batch) and the detected-failure
latch reported as "diag" on /status:

    sh tools/test_log_capture.sh


Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
